From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shayne Legault <8741557+shaynelegault@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:20:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] ARM: dts: apple: Drop the read-only note from the P105
 flash controller

The H2FMI driver now erases blocks for SFTL reclamation, so the flash
controller is no longer read-only.

[Henrik: keep the shared compatible; the driver follows the discovered
 package geometry instead of a P105 compatible]

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Shayne Legault <8741557+shaynelegault@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/apple/s5l8942x-p105.dts | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/apple/s5l8942x-p105.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/apple/s5l8942x-p105.dts
index f4fe413..fe2e18c 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/apple/s5l8942x-p105.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/apple/s5l8942x-p105.dts
@@ -692,7 +692,8 @@
 		 * known -- a NAND reset drops the PPN to SDR and only a reboot
 		 * through iBEC gets DDR back.
 		 *
-		 * Read-only.  See docs/research/p105-nand.md. */
+		 * See docs/research/p105-nand.md.
+		 */
 		nand: flash-controller@1200000 {
 			compatible = "apple,s5l8940x-fmi";
 			reg = <0x1200000 0x1000>,	/* FMI0 */
